   $q$Which evidence did Fenwick use to show that electric lights could make streets safer?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The debate filled the town hall for two full nights.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The electric company had been formed only four months earlier.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speakers"},{"text":"Dalton's wagon accidents after dark fell from 23 to 9 in one year.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Six shop owners promised to stay open two hours later.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Dalton's wagon accidents after dark fell from 23 to 9 in one year.$q$, $q$Fewer accidents after dark is evidence about safety. The shop owners' promise supports a different point, that lights would help business.$q$, 'draft', '1320f481-cf9c-5b60-9035-011cd5957c22')
