   $q$How does the author respond to council members who want to spend the money on road repair?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author argues the program is so small a cost that ending it would barely help the roads.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author argues that the roads in Ridgeview do not need any repair.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The author agrees and suggests ending the program after one more year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The author suggests that teenagers could repair the roads each summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author argues the program is so small a cost that ending it would barely help the roads.$q$, $q$The author says the program "costs less than one percent" of the maintenance budget, so cutting it "would barely change the condition of the roads." The author admits "Roads matter," so the author does not deny that roads need repair.$q$, 'draft', '1234fd4d-f2ca-5e66-9c39-f11c37341b24')
